WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.712 --> 00:00:06.450
One flip card per course concept: the concept in front, the definition behind.

2
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:16.159
Try to answer before you flip. Recalling before revealing is what makes flashcards work. Guessing first, even wrongly, strengthens the memory.

3
00:00:16.159 --> 00:00:22.767
Filter by week. Before a Knowledge Check, run the cards for that week plus one earlier week.

4
00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:33.771
Work the Self-Check Studio. With a week selected, the studio pairs that week's Western and Indigenous readings as two attributed eyes, gives you a quick check, and can save a Word record of your work.

5
00:00:33.771 --> 00:00:41.682
Say the definition out loud in your own words. If you can only repeat the card's wording, flip it again tomorrow.

6
00:00:41.682 --> 00:00:46.189
Cards and the studio are pure practice. Nothing is scored.

7
00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:50.998
Where next: Take the week's Knowledge Check and see what stuck.
